WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.391
Childhood cancer is not
simply adult cancer occurring earlier.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.054
The supplied chapter emphasizes
immature tissues and developmental origins.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.872
Compare two paths.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.783
In one, immature cells mature and differentiate.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.853
In the embryonal-tumor model,
tissue fails to differentiate and

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.180
retains an immature pattern.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.629
Many childhood cancers arise from mesodermal tissues.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.660
Growth timing, inherited factors
and exposures belong to the

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.935
same assessment; no single factor explains every case.
